@startuml
title Wait and approval suspension lifecycle
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #ECF5FC
  BorderColor #477B9B
  StartColor #2F7C5A
  EndColor #7D478F
  ArrowColor #496174
}

state "Suspended run" as Suspended #FFF0D9 {
  state "Signal wait\nwait:{token}:{node}" as SignalWait #FFF0D9
  state "Event wait\nwait:{token}:{node}" as EventWait #FFF0D9
  state "Timer wait\nwait:{token}:{node}" as TimerWait #FFF0D9
  state "Retry wait\nretry:{token}:{attempt}" as RetryWait #FFE0C8
  state "Durable-yield wait\nyield:{token}:{transition}\ndueAt = park instant" as YieldWait #F8DADA
  state "Approval\napproval:{token}:{node}" as Approval #FFE0C8 {
    state "Collecting decisions" as Collecting #FFE0C8
    [*] --> Collecting
    Collecting --> Collecting : approve [<latex>|D| < q</latex>]\n/ record unique decisionId,\nemit approvalRecorded
  }
}

state "Resumed in Route phase\n(disposition completed)" as ResumedCompleted #D9EFDF
state "Resumed in Route phase\n(disposition rejected)" as ResumedRejected #E7DCF5
state "Resumed in Route phase\n(disposition timedOut)" as ResumedTimedOut #FBE8D4
state "Re-entered in Enter phase" as ReEntered #E9F5EA
state "Cancelled\n(compensation unwinds)" as Cancelled #E7DCF5

SignalWait --> ResumedCompleted : signal [name matches]\n/ payload replaces value
EventWait --> ResumedCompleted : event [name matches]\n/ payload replaces value
TimerWait --> ResumedCompleted : timerFired\n[<latex>d = d_{\mathrm{expected}} \;\land\; \mathrm{now} \ge d</latex>]\nscheduler self-signs at expiry
Collecting --> ResumedCompleted : approve [<latex>|D| \ge q</latex>]\n/ waitSatisfied, approvalRecorded, runResumed
Collecting --> ResumedRejected : reject [actor is an approver]\n/ disposition rejected
Collecting --> ResumedTimedOut : timerFired [deadline expired]\nby scheduler / no approvalRecorded,\nlate decisions answer\n"wait ... is not pending"
RetryWait --> ReEntered : timerFired [exact deadline]\nor retry command\n/ attempt + 1, node re-executes
YieldWait --> ReEntered : timerFired [dueAt = park instant]\nby scheduler / target entered;\nevents durableYield, waitSatisfied,\nrunResumed
Suspended --> Cancelled : cancel command (run level)

note bottom of Approval #FFF3C9
An empty approver set admits any ledger-authorized
actor. Each actor decides at most once and every
decisionId is globally unique. The approval deadline
(from the node timeout policy) is recorded, published
as the run's due_at, and enforced: at expiry the
recovery scheduler self-signs timerFired and the wait
resumes with disposition timedOut. Publish validation
requires a timedOut route wherever a timeout is
declared (approval-timeout-unrouted).
end note
note left of TimerWait #EAF7EE
A timer whose deadline expression cannot be
computed never parks: the token routes failed
with value {error, deadline}, readable through
the error value root. Literal deadlines are
rejected at publish time unless they parse
(invalid-timer-deadline-literal).
end note
@enduml
